<%= UiComponents::Lookbook::TableOfContents.call(page) %>

The trigger and action element used across components. Renders a `<button>`, or an `<a>` when
given `href:`.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/button)

<%= embed UI::ButtonPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
Button { "Save" }
Button(variant: :outline, size: :sm) { "Cancel" }
Button(href: "/docs", variant: :ghost) { "Read the docs" }
```

## Examples

### Variants

`variant:` picks the visual style: `primary` (default), `primary_outline`, `secondary`, `soft`,
`outline`, `ghost` and `destructive`.

<%= embed UI::ButtonPreview, :variants %>

### Sizes & icon buttons

`size:` scales height, padding, radius and icon size. `icon: true` makes a square button - give
it an `aria_label:`. Mark a leading or trailing icon with `data: { icon: "start" }` /
`data: { icon: "end" }` to tighten the padding on that side.

<%= embed UI::ButtonPreview, :sizes %>

```ruby
Button(variant: :soft, icon: true, aria_label: "Bookmark") { bookmark_icon }

Button do
  svg(data: { icon: "start" }, ...) { |s| s.path(d: "...") }
  plain "Rename workspace"
end
```

### As another component's trigger

Parts like `DrawerTrigger` and `DrawerClose` yield their attributes to a block, so a Button can
be the element they render (Appica's `render={<Button />}`):

```ruby
DrawerTrigger { |trigger| Button(**trigger, variant: :outline) { "Open drawer" } }
```

The part's `data-slot` wins over Button's, so styling hooks like `[data-slot=drawer-close]` keep working.

## API reference

### Button

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `variant:` | `:primary`, `:primary_outline`, `:secondary`, `:soft`, `:outline`, `:ghost`, `:destructive` | `:primary` | Visual style. |
| `size:` | `:sm`, `:md`, `:lg` | `:md` | Height, padding, radius and icon size. |
| `icon:` | `Boolean` | `false` | Square icon-only button. |
| `href:` | `String` | - | Render an `<a>` instead of a `<button>`. |
| `type:` | `String` | `"button"` | Button type; pass `"submit"` inside forms. |
| `class:` | `String` | - | Extra classes, merged via tailwind_merge. |

Any other attributes (`disabled:`, `aria_label:`, `data:`, …) go on the element.

## Accessibility

- Icon-only buttons need an accessible name: `aria_label:`.
- Disabled buttons use the native `disabled` attribute, so they're skipped by keyboard focus.
- Use `href:` for navigation and a button for actions, so assistive tech announces the right role.
